{"name":"Livingstone","hex":"#cbcbbb","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Livingstone","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A Scottish surname from Old English, variant of Livingston.","A city in Southern Province, Zambia, named after David Livingstone."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Livingstone"}],"entries":[{"title":"Livingstone (name)","blocks":[{"text":"Livingstone is a surname and given name. The surname is toponymic. It is one of the habitual surnames eventually adopted by members of the Scottish branch of the Irish Dunleavy /MacNulty royals, including the ancestors of the African missionary doctor and African explorer David Livingstone. There may be a relationship between the Livingstones and Clan MacLea."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/David_Livingstone_by_Thomas_Annan.jpg/330px-David_Livingstone_by_Thomas_Annan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Livingstone_(name)","wikidata":"Q21751041"},{"title":"David Livingstone","blocks":[{"text":"David Livingstone was a Scottish doctor, Congregationalist, pioneer Christian missionary with the London Missionary Society, and an explorer in Africa. Livingstone was married to Mary Moffat Livingstone, from the prominent 18th-century Moffat missionary family. Livingstone came to have a mythic status as a Protestant missionary martyr, working-class \"rags-to-riches\" inspirational story, scientific investigator and explorer, imperial reformer, anti-slavery crusader, and advocate of British commercial and colonial expansion. As a result, he became one of the most popular British heroes of the late 19th-century Victorian era."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/David_Livingstone_by_Thomas_Annan.jpg/330px-David_Livingstone_by_Thomas_Annan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/David_Livingstone","wikidata":"Q48373"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Birthplace_of_david_livingstone.jpg/330px-Birthplace_of_david_livingstone.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Birthplace_of_david_livingstone.jpg/330px-Birthplace_of_david_livingstone.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Livingstone's birthplace in Blantyre, South Lanarkshire, Scotland","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABirthplace_of_david_livingstone.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/David_Livingstones_birthplace_%28geograph_4530192%29.jpg/500px-David_Livingstones_birthplace_%28geograph_4530192%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/David_Livingstones_birthplace_%28geograph_4530192%29.jpg/500px-David_Livingstones_birthplace_%28geograph_4530192%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"David Livingstone's birthplace, with period furnishings","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADavid_Livingstones_birthplace_(geograph_4530192).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Dance_of_Landeens.jpg/500px-Dance_of_Landeens.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Dance_of_Landeens.jpg/500px-Dance_of_Landeens.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Zulu dance, at Shupanga on the Zambesi, to collect tribute from Portuguese merchants","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADance_of_Landeens.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/David_Livingstone_attacked_by_a_lion_in_Africa._Lithograph._Wellcome_V0018847.jpg/500px-David_Livingstone_attacked_by_a_lion_in_Africa._Lithograph._Wellcome_V0018847.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/David_Livingstone_attacked_by_a_lion_in_Africa._Lithograph._Wellcome_V0018847.jpg/1280px-David_Livingstone_attacked_by_a_lion_in_Africa._Lithograph._Wellcome_V0018847.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/David_Livingstone_attacked_by_a_lion_in_Africa._Lithograph._Wellcome_V0018847.jpg/500px-David_Livingstone_attacked_by_a_lion_in_Africa._Lithograph._Wellcome_V0018847.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Deacon Mebalwe shooting, distracting the lion which had overpowered Livingstone","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADavid_Livingstone_attacked_by_a_lion_in_Africa._Lithograph._Wellcome_V0018847.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Livingstone_and_the_Lion.jpg/500px-Livingstone_and_the_Lion.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Livingstone_and_the_Lion.jpg/1280px-Livingstone_and_the_Lion.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Livingstone_and_the_Lion.jpg/500px-Livingstone_and_the_Lion.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Livingstone Memorial Sculpture in Blantyre, Scotland","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALivingstone_and_the_Lion.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Preaching_from_a_Waggon_%28David_Livingstone%29_by_The_London_Missionary_Society.jpg/500px-Preaching_from_a_Waggon_%28David_Livingstone%29_by_The_London_Missionary_Society.jpg?utm_